claims:
1. A computer-implemented method comprising:
capturing an image at a client device, the image compris- ing a depiction of an object;
identifying the object within the image, the identifying the object within the image comprising:
identifying a first set of image features within the image;
storing the first set of features in an indexing structure;
identifying a second set of image features based on the first set of image features by mapping each feature in the first set of image features to a representative feature in a set of representative features;
searching the indexing structure using the second set of image features;
accessing media content associated with the object in response to identifying the object within the image;
accessing a media template, the media template defining a set of presentation positions within a graphical user interface of the client device, the set of presentation positions based on a position of the identified objec- tions within the image; and
in response to verifying the accessed media content, causing presentation of the media content within the image at the client device based on the accessed media template.

